sentences.t:
Plogo a Álbar Fáñez de lo que dixo don Rodrigo.
A este don Jero[me] yal otorgan por obispo;
diéronle en Valencia o bien puede estar rico.

sentences.l:
It-pleased to Álbar Fáñez of what said don Rodrigo.
To this don Jero[me] now-him they-grant as bishop;
they-gave-him in Valencia where well he-can be rich.

sentences.t:
Essora dixo el rey: “Plazme de coraçon[e];
yo les mandaré dar conducho mientra que por mi tierra f[o]ren,
de fonta e de mal curial[l]as e de desonor[e];

sentences.l:
Then said the king: “It-pleases-me from heart;
I to-them will-order to-give provisions while that through my land they-shall-be,
from outrage and from harm to-guard-them and from dishonour;

sentences.t:
Oídme, escuelas, e toda la mi cort!
non quiero que nada pierda el Campeador;
a todas las escuelas que a él dizen señor
por que los deseredé, todo gelo suelto yo;

sentences.l:
Hear-me, retinues, and all the my court!
not I-want that anything may-lose the Campeador;
to all the retinues which to him say lord
for which them I-disinherited, all to-them-it release I;

let-serve-them' their estates where may-be the Campeador,
I-guarantee-them the bodies from harm and from mischance,
for such I-do this that they-may-serve to their lord.”

sentences.t:
Minaya Álbar Fáñez al buen rey se espidió.
“¿Hya vos ides, Minaya? id a la graçia del Criador!
Levedes un portero, tengo que vos avrá pro;

sentences.l:
Minaya Álbar Fáñez to-the good king himself took-leave.
“Already you go, Minaya? go to the grace of-the Creator!
You-should-take a porter, I-hold that to-you it-will-have profit;
